### Manual Testing with CURL

**Register:**
```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/auth/register \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{
    "name": "Test User",
    "email": "test@example.com",
    "password": "password123",
    "phone": "1234567890",
    "location_lat": 40.7128,
    "location_long": -74.0060,
    "roles": ["donor"]
  }'
```

**Login:**
```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/auth/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email": "test@example.com", "password": "password123"}'
```

**Protected Route:**
```bash
curl -X GET http://127.0.0.1:5000/food/all \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer <your-token>"
```

## Error Handling

### Standard Error Response
```json
{
  "success": false,
  "error": "Error message",
  "details": "Additional details (optional)"
}
```

### HTTP Status Codes
- `200` - Success
- `201` - Created
- `400` - Bad Request
- `401` - Unauthorized
- `403` - Forbidden (insufficient permissions)
- `404` - Not Found
- `500` - Internal Server Error

## Logging

### Enable Debug Logging
```python
import logging
logging.basicConfig(level=logging.DEBUG)
```

### Custom Logging
```python
app.logger.info("User registered: %s", user_id)
app.logger.error("Database error: %s", str(error))
```

## Environment Variables for Production
```env
FLASK_ENV=production
FLASK_DEBUG=False
DATABASE_URL=<production-postgres-url>
MONGODB_URI=<production-mongo-url>
JWT_SECRET_KEY=<strong-random-secret>
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://yourdomain.com
```

## Security Checklist
- [ ] Change `JWT_SECRET_KEY` to strong random value
- [ ] Set `FLASK_DEBUG=False`
- [ ] Use HTTPS only
- [ ] Restrict CORS origins
- [ ] Enable rate limiting
- [ ] Use connection pooling
- [ ] Set up database backups
- [ ] Monitor logs

## Troubleshooting

### Database Connection Issues
```bash
# Test PostgreSQL connection
psql -U username -d frns_db -c "SELECT 1;"

# Check DATABASE_URL format
echo $DATABASE_URL
```

### JWT Token Issues
```bash
# Verify token
python troubleshoot.py

# Check token expiry
python -c "import jwt; print(jwt.decode('token', verify=False))"
```

### MongoDB Not Available
- App continues without MongoDB
- Check `MONGODB_URI` in `.env`
- Verify MongoDB is running: `mongo --eval "db.adminCommand('ping')"`

### Socket.IO Connection Failed
- Ensure Socket.IO origins are allowed
- Check client is sending JWT in connection query
- Verify port 5000 is accessible

## Development Tips

### Hot Reload
Flask auto-reloads on code changes in debug mode.

### Database Reset (Development)
```bash
flask db downgrade base
flask db upgrade
```

### View All Routes
```python
for rule in app.url_map.iter_rules():
    print(f"{rule.endpoint}: {rule.methods} {rule.rule}")
```